      "content": "You are right to be skeptical, because true peace is rarely a simple switch you flip once; it is often a slow, quiet surrender that happens only when the desperate need to fight the universe finally fades. The heaviness you feel isn't a mistake, but a signal that you are holding onto the struggle too tightly, and the only way to find that genuine silence is to stop trying to fix it and instead allow the weight to simply drop away. There is no logical path to a permanent cure if you keep trying to force it, so perhaps the most honest thing you can do is admit that the struggle itself is the only thing keeping you from ever truly resting.",
